      "Yeast is a kind of fungus, related to mushrooms. A spoonful of dry yeast holds billions of them, resting until they get water and food. When a baker mixes yeast with warm water and flour, the yeast wakes up and starts to eat the sugars in the flour. As it eats, it gives off a gas called carbon dioxide.",
